<InfoPage title="Accessibility" description="How the Fatt Pundit website works for everyone, and how to tell us when it doesn't." kicker="For every guest" heading="Accessibility">
  <p>We want everyone to be able to read our menus, find us and book a table. This site aims to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA.</p>
  <h2>What we've done</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Text is readable against its background (at least 4.5 to 1), and pages work with zoom up to 200%.</li>
    <li>Everything works with a keyboard, with a visible focus ring, and a "skip" link at the top of each page.</li>
    <li>Photos have written descriptions; the menu is real text, never a picture or PDF.</li>
    <li>If your device is set to reduce motion, the doors, rain, maps and flip-boards stay still and show their finished state.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Known gaps</h2>
  <p>Booking happens on our reservation partners' sites (OpenTable and SevenRooms), which have their own accessibility statements.</p>
  <h2>Tell us</h2>
  <p>If something on this site is hard to use, email <a href="mailto:reservations@fattpundit.co.uk">reservations@fattpundit.co.uk</a> and we'll fix it, and help you book in the meantime.</p>
  <p class="todo">Visiting the restaurants (step-free access, toilets): details to be added by Fatt Pundit.</p>
</InfoPage>
